{"title":"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The smallest number in the list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b125c3db08211dc85ddf65fd79cee772be6cb48e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1.0101, 1.0011, 1.0110, 1.1001, 1.1100\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"305\" height=\"20\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19df1de78a607b18b47ec5bfa6ad659bddd973fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 1.0101 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 1.0011 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 1.0110 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 1.1001 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 1.1100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"595\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All of the numbers are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we can look at the tenths and hundredths digits.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d05e113ac4e14821e2cac65c9f245a9bcaa01e79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.0101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541d8cb07e06fc072d8fc107b2db47510bfa4915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.0011$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2aecc69f3e618c36fb71dc3729e9254e910d69e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.0110$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> would have to be the smallest numbers because the other two numbers have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the tenths place. \n</p><p>Of these numbers, the smallest is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/0/960f0a2be07519fe0b943782e15c33ac94b63bde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 1.0011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"98\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#16